# Article full texts. The review may read them, it may not redistribute them, so
# no individual article body is carried in Git. What is carried is the inventory,
# the identifiers, and everything the coding derived from the text: the coded
# rows, the extracted items, the verbatim evidence quotes, and the aggregate
# tables. An authorized reviewer restores the texts locally with
# `make fulltext-corpus`, which repeats retrieval and quote verification.
src/06_review_stages/04_extraction/inputs/fulltext_cache/
src/05_data/pilot/02_fulltext_level/01_corpus/03_fulltext_txt/*
!src/05_data/pilot/02_fulltext_level/01_corpus/03_fulltext_txt/.gitkeep

# Local vector store for semantic label matching. The embeddings are a cache of
# the OpenRouter embedding endpoint keyed by label text: regenerating them is one
# command and a fraction of a cent, so the vectors are not carried in Git.
src/05_data/interim/embeddings/

# Internal working sections, kept local and never published. 07_docs holds the
# project status write-ups, 08_artifacts is scratch space for run logs and
# validation. Neither carries review data: the committed record of a run lives
# under src/05_data and src/06_review_stages.
src/07_docs/
src/08_artifacts/
